      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is incredibly annoying, and you are right, it feels like digital pest control, but these \"pests\" are often highly organized, low-level operations. The absurdity of the small amounts is precisely what makes them so effective, as they fly under the radar of standard monitoring tools. To stop them, you need to move beyond just looking at the total value and start looking at the *behavior*—the frequency and the destination patterns.\n\nYou must implement stricter, real-time monitoring thresholds that flag any outgoing transaction to an unwhitelisted address, regardless of the amount. If the smart contract allows for external calls that aren't strictly necessary for its core function, that's a potential weak point that needs immediate patching. This is less about stopping a single big thief and more about sealing every tiny crack in the digital wall.",
